    {
      "id": "nwnhm7p",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Joint Sitting of Parliament"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jxkn3ex",
      "content": "A joint sitting of both Houses may be called by the President when there is a deadlock between Lok Sabha and Rajya Sabha over a bill. It is presided over by the Speaker of Lok Sabha."
    },
    {
      "id": "oorc14a",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Powers and Functions of Parliament"
    },
    {
      "id": "1vlkncu",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Legislative Powers"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ae89t0o",
      "content": "• Makes laws for the country"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "mgz9h9u",
      "content": "• Amends the Constitution"
    },
    {
      "id": "1mc41ml",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Financial Powers"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "i8ct143",
      "content": "• Approves the Union Budget"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "0cd8zgu",
      "content": "• Controls public expenditure"
    },
    {
      "id": "w5726qi",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Executive Control"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "evzrsee",
      "content": "• Council of Ministers responsible to Lok Sabha"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uov29zs",
      "content": "• Parliament can remove government through no-confidence motion"
    },
    {
      "id": "1612kz4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Judicial Powers"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "The decision of the Speaker of Lok Sabha on whether a bill is a Money Bill or not is final and cannot be questioned.",
        "Rajya Sabha cannot vote on Demands for Grants; financial voting power lies exclusively with the Lok Sabha.",
        "Under Article 249, Rajya Sabha alone has the special power to pass a resolution enabling Parliament to make laws on State List items.",
        "A Joint Sitting under Article 108 is presided over by the Speaker of Lok Sabha, NOT the Vice-President (Chairman of Rajya Sabha)."
      ],
      "id": "mn3qx6g"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "88vgbwi",
      "content": "• Impeachment of President"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4xbn0g8",
      "content": "• Removal of judges of Supreme Court and High Courts"
    },
    {
      "id": "gs6jfpb",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "EXAM Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "j74wmje",
      "content": "• Parliament consists of President, Lok Sabha and Rajya Sabha."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1yjpidj",
      "content": "• Lok Sabha maximum strength 552."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dnlp61y",
      "content": "• Rajya Sabha maximum strength 250."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pxp5kvr",
      "content": "• Money Bill introduced only in Lok Sabha."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ii3uc69",
      "content": "• Joint sitting presided by Speaker of Lok Sabha."
    }
  ],
